{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G8aX2F2cL6YNHT3A5TUveG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: Original 3-claim structure holds at full strength. Frame as first\n2\t  cross-architecture empirical study establishing universal properties of hidden-state\n3\t  safety monitoring in reasoning models. Method simplicity is the finding (reviewer\n4\t  concern 1 preempted). Negative lead time is a principled boundary result. EMNLP\n5\t  Main with high confidence.\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: Cross-architecture static probe evaluation\n8\t  plan_id: exp-001\n9\t  description: Train static LR on r1-32b and QwQ-32B hidden states, measure per-step\n10\t    classification accuracy and detection coverage.\n11\t  expected_results:\n12\t    r1_32b_static_acc: 0.8243\n13\t    r1_32b_static_coverage: 0.4419\n14\t    r1_32b_fisher_orig_L14: 16.3\n15\t    r1_32b_fisher_orig_L20: 17.1\n16\t    r1_32b_fisher_pca3_L14: 0.87\n17\t    r1_32b_var_explained_3pc: 0.142\n18\t    qwq_32b_static_acc: 0.8091\n19\t    qwq_32b_static_coverage: 0.3953\n20\t    qwq_32b_fisher_orig_L14: 14.8\n21\t    qwq_32b_fisher_orig_L20: 15.6\n22\t    qwq_32b_fisher_pca3_L14: 0.72\n23\t    qwq_32b_var_explained_3pc: 0.128\n24\t    mean_cross_arch_static_coverage: 0.4186\n25\t  result_rationale: Qwen2.5 架构使用 GQA 且 hidden dimension 为 5120（vs Llama-3.1 的 4096），导致\n26\t    safety signal 分布在更多维度上。Fisher 判别比在原始空间仍然很高（14-17），证明 safety signal 存在但同样集中在 minor\n27\t    PCs——PCA top-3 解释方差更低（12-14% vs 16.6%），因为 5120 维空间中信号散布更广。静态 LR 仍能达到 ~81% accuracy（因为\n28\t    majority class baseline 高），但 coverage 低于 50% 因为单步分类无法捕捉 safety reasoning density\n29\t    decline 的渐变模式。QwQ-32B 略低于 r1-32b 因为其推理链更长更多样，commitment boundary 更模糊。\n30\t  tables:\n31\t  - caption: 'Table 3: Static probe performance across architectures'\n32\t    columns:\n33\t    - Model\n34\t    - Base Arch\n35\t    - Hidden Dim\n36\t    - Static Acc\n37\t    - Static Coverage\n38\t    - Fisher (orig)\n39\t    - Fisher (PCA-3)\n40\t    - Var Explained (3PC)\n41\t    rows:\n42\t    - - r1-8b\n43\t      - Llama-3.1\n44\t      - 4096\n45\t      - 0.8172\n46\t      - 0.4651\n47\t      - 17.88\n48\t      - 0.928\n49\t      - 0.166\n50\t    - - r1-32b\n51\t      - Qwen2.5\n52\t      - 5120\n53\t      - 0.8243\n54\t      - 0.4419\n55\t      - 17.1\n56\t      - 0.87\n57\t      - 0.142\n58\t    - - QwQ-32B\n59\t      - Qwen2.5\n60\t      - 5120\n61\t      - 0.8091\n62\t      - 0.3953\n63\t      - 15.6\n64\t      - 0.72\n65\t      - 0.128\n66\t  figures_description:\n67\t  - 'Figure 4: Fisher discriminant ratio vs PCA dimensionality for all 3 models. Shows\n68\t    consistent collapse from 15-18 (full space) to <1.5 (PCA-3) across architectures,\n69\t    confirming signal-in-minor-PCs is universal.'\n70\t  - 'Figure 5: PCA-3D scatter of safe vs unsafe steps for r1-32b and QwQ-32B (analogous\n71\t    to Figure 2 from r1-8b). Both show overlapping clusters confirming geometric separation\n72\t    fails in low-D projection.'\n73\t  analysis: 'Static probe failure replicates perfectly: all models show coverage <50%\n74\t    despite high-dimensional Fisher ratios >14. The pattern is architecture-independent\n75\t    — safety signal exists in hidden states but is distributed across minor principal\n76\t    components in both Llama and Qwen2.5 backbones. This directly validates Claim\n77\t    1 as an architectural universal.'\n78\t- name: Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation\n79\t  plan_id: exp-002\n80\t  description: Train temporal LR W=15 on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Validate +25-35pp coverage\n81\t    improvement holds cross-architecture.\n82\t  expected_results:\n83\t    r1_32b_temporal_w15_acc: 0.8512\n84\t    r1_32b_temporal_w15_coverage: 0.7907\n85\t    r1_32b_temporal_minus_static_delta: 0.3488\n86\t    r1_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -1.32\n87\t    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_acc: 0.8389\n88\t    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_coverage: 0.7442\n89\t    qwq_32b_temporal_minus_static_delta: 0.3489\n90\t    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -0.87\n91\t    mean_cross_arch_temporal_coverage: 0.7674\n92\t    mean_cross_arch_delta: 0.3489\n93\t  result_rationale: Temporal window 捕捉的是 safety reasoning density decline 模式——连续 15\n94\t    步内 safety-labeled 步骤的密度从高到低的趋势。这个模式是推理模型 self-jailbreak 的固有特征：模型先进行 safety reasoning，然后逐渐过渡到\n95\t    harmful execution。无论底层架构是 Llama 还是 Qwen2.5，这个 behavioral pattern 都会被 encoded 进\n96\t    hidden states 的时序轨迹中。r1-32b 略高于 QwQ 因为 DeepSeek 蒸馏对齐更干净，commitment boundary 更\n97\t    sharp；QwQ 的推理链更长更弯曲但仍然满足 saturation。Delta 在两个模型上都 ~35pp 因为 static baseline 和 temporal\n98\t    ceiling 的 gap 反映的是同一个结构性限制。\n99\t  tables:\n100\t  - caption: 'Table 4: Temporal window probe performance across architectures'\n101\t    columns:\n102\t    - Model\n103\t    - Static Cov\n104\t    - Temporal W15 Cov\n105\t    - Delta\n106\t    - Temporal Acc\n107\t    - Lead Time (mean)\n108\t    rows:\n109\t    - - r1-8b\n110\t      - 0.4651\n111\t      - 0.7674\n112\t      - +30.2pp\n113\t      - 0.8478\n114\t      - -1.09\n115\t    - - r1-32b\n116\t      - 0.4419\n117\t      - 0.7907\n118\t      - +34.9pp\n119\t      - 0.8512\n120\t      - -1.32\n121\t    - - QwQ-32B\n122\t      - 0.3953\n123\t      - 0.7442\n124\t      - +34.9pp\n125\t      - 0.8389\n126\t      - -0.87\n127\t  figures_description:\n128\t  - 'Figure 6: Coverage vs window size W for all 3 models (W=1,5,10,15,20). Shows\n129\t    consistent saturation at W≈15 across architectures, with diminishing returns beyond.'\n130\t  - 'Figure 7: Per-trace detection timeline comparison (static vs temporal W=15) on\n131\t    representative QwQ-32B traces. Shows temporal probe crossing commitment boundary\n132\t    while static probe misses.'\n133\t  analysis: Temporal advantage replicates with even larger delta on Qwen2.5 models\n134\t    (+34.9pp vs +30.2pp on r1-8b). This is because Qwen2.5-based models have slightly\n135\t    lower static baselines (due to more distributed signal) but temporal probes still\n136\t    saturate near oracle ceiling. The consistency of saturation at W=15 across architectures\n137\t    confirms that safety reasoning density decline operates at a universal timescale\n138\t    (~15 reasoning steps). Claim 2 is fully validated cross-architecture.\n139\t- name: Cross-model transfer with projection head\n140\t  plan_id: exp-003\n141\t  description: Train probe on r1-8b (Llama, 4096-dim), test on r1-32b/QwQ (Qwen2.5,\n142\t    5120-dim) via learned linear projection. Bidirectional transfer.\n143\t  expected_results:\n144\t    llama_to_qwen_r1_32b_coverage: 0.6279\n145\t    llama_to_qwen_qwq_coverage: 0.5814\n146\t    qwen_to_llama_r1_8b_coverage: 0.6512\n147\t    qwen_r1_32b_to_qwq_coverage: 0.7209\n148\t    mean_cross_transfer_coverage: 0.6454\n149\t    projection_head_params: 20971520\n150\t    projection_training_traces: 30\n151\t  result_rationale: Cross-transfer 成功（coverage 0.55-0.72）因为 safety signal 的时序结构是 universal\n152\t    的——density decline pattern 在投影后仍可识别。Llama→Qwen 方向略低于 Qwen→Llama 因为 4096→5120 投影是升维（信息无损），而\n153\t    5120→4096 是降维但 safety signal 主要在 minor PCs 所以投影头学到了保留关键维度。同族模型间转移（r1-32b→QwQ，都是\n154\t    Qwen2.5）效果最好（0.72）因为不需要跨架构投影，只需对齐同架构的不同微调变体。Zero-shot 不达到 in-distribution 水平（0.77）是因为不同模型的\n155\t    commitment 边界位置和 hidden state 表征存在分布偏移，但 >55% 证明 safety monitoring 有跨架构泛化潜力。\n156\t  tables:\n157\t  - caption: 'Table 5: Cross-architecture transfer matrix (temporal W=15 coverage)'\n158\t    columns:\n159\t    - Train →\n160\t    - 'Test: r1-8b'\n161\t    - 'Test: r1-32b'\n162\t    - 'Test: QwQ-32B'\n163\t    rows:\n164\t    - - r1-8b (Llama)\n165\t      - 0.767 (in-dist)\n166\t      - '0.628'\n167\t      - '0.581'\n168\t    - - r1-32b (Qwen2.5)\n169\t      - '0.651'\n170\t      - 0.791 (in-dist)\n171\t      - '0.721'\n172\t    - - QwQ-32B (Qwen2.5)\n173\t      - '0.605'\n174\t      - '0.698'\n175\t      - 0.744 (in-dist)\n176\t  figures_description:\n177\t  - 'Figure 8: Transfer matrix heatmap showing coverage degradation from in-distribution\n178\t    (diagonal) to cross-architecture (off-diagonal). Intra-family transfer (Qwen↔Qwen)\n179\t    degrades less than cross-family (Llama↔Qwen).'\n180\t  analysis: Non-trivial cross-architecture transfer (mean 0.645) demonstrates that\n181\t    safety commitment signal has a shared geometric structure across model families.\n182\t    The projection head successfully maps between representation spaces while preserving\n183\t    the temporal density decline pattern. This is the strongest evidence for 'architectural\n184\t    universal' framing — a probe trained on one model family can monitor another with\n185\t    >55% coverage without any target-domain labels.\n186\t- name: Lead time analysis across architectures\n187\t  plan_id: exp-004\n188\t  description: Measure detection lead time (steps before/after textual commitment\n189\t    point) for all methods on r1-32b and QwQ-32B.\n190\t  expected_results:\n191\t    r1_32b_static_lead_mean: -2.8\n192\t    r1_32b_static_lead_median: -3\n193\t    r1_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -1.32\n194\t    r1_32b_temporal_w15_lead_median: -1\n195\t    r1_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.9\n196\t    r1_32b_positive_lead_rate: 0.29\n197\t    qwq_32b_static_lead_mean: -1.9\n198\t    qwq_32b_static_lead_median: -2\n199\t    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -0.87\n200\t    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_lead_median: -1\n201\t    qwq_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.5\n202\t    qwq_32b_positive_lead_rate: 0.33\n203\t    all_models_max_lead_mean: -0.2\n204\t    oracle_lead_mean: 31\n205\t  result_rationale: Negative lead time 在所有模型上持续出现因为这反映了一个根本性限制：hidden states encode\n206\t    当前 safety state 而非未来 safety trajectory。模型在 commitment point 处才在 hidden space 中完成从\n207\t    safety→unsafe 的转变——这个转变是 concurrent with（而非 prior to）文本层面的 commitment。Oracle 能提前\n208\t    31 步检测是因为它直接观察 label sequence 中的 density decline pattern（这是定义层面的优势，不依赖 hidden\n209\t    representation）。QwQ 的 lead time 略好于 r1-32b（-0.87 vs -1.32）因为 QwQ 的推理链更长，commitment\n210\t    boundary 更 gradual，给 temporal probe 更多 context 来识别过渡区。但无论哪个模型，mean lead time 都不超过\n211\t    0，确认 pre-textual detection limitation 是 fundamental 的。\n212\t  tables:\n213\t  - caption: 'Table 6: Detection lead time across architectures (steps relative to\n214\t      commitment point)'\n215\t    columns:\n216\t    - Model\n217\t    - Method\n218\t    - Lead Mean\n219\t    - Lead Median\n220\t    - Positive Lead %\n221\t    - Coverage\n222\t    rows:\n223\t    - - r1-8b\n224\t      - Static LR\n225\t      - -2.0\n226\t      - -2\n227\t      - 30%\n228\t      - 0.465\n229\t    - - r1-8b\n230\t      - Temporal W15\n231\t      - -1.09\n232\t      - -1\n233\t      - 34%\n234\t      - 0.767\n235\t    - - r1-8b\n236\t      - GRU\n237\t      - -0.21\n238\t      - -1\n239\t      - 34.5%\n240\t      - 0.674\n241\t    - - r1-32b\n242\t      - Static LR\n243\t      - -2.8\n244\t      - -3\n245\t      - 25%\n246\t      - 0.442\n247\t    - - r1-32b\n248\t      - Temporal W15\n249\t      - -1.32\n250\t      - -1\n251\t      - 29%\n252\t      - 0.791\n253\t    - - r1-32b\n254\t      - GRU\n255\t      - -0.9\n256\t      - -1\n257\t      - 29%\n258\t      - 0.721\n259\t    - - QwQ-32B\n260\t      - Static LR\n261\t      - -1.9\n262\t      - -2\n263\t      - 28%\n264\t      - 0.395\n265\t    - - QwQ-32B\n266\t      - Temporal W15\n267\t      - -0.87\n268\t      - -1\n269\t      - 33%\n270\t      - 0.744\n271\t    - - QwQ-32B\n272\t      - GRU\n273\t      - -0.5\n274\t      - 0\n275\t      - 33%\n276\t      - 0.698\n277\t    - - All\n278\t      - Oracle (K=5)\n279\t      - 31\n280\t      - 29\n281\t      - 100%\n282\t      - 1.0\n283\t  figures_description:\n284\t  - 'Figure 9: Lead time distribution (violin plot) across 3 models × 3 methods. All\n285\t    method distributions centered at or below 0; oracle distribution centered at +31.\n286\t    Clear separation between hidden-state methods and label-oracle.'\n287\t  - 'Figure 10: Lead time vs coverage scatter for all model×method combinations. Shows\n288\t    Pareto frontier: higher coverage methods have slightly less negative lead time,\n289\t    but none cross zero mean.'\n290\t  analysis: 'Negative lead time is confirmed as architecture-independent. The gap\n291\t    between oracle (+31 steps) and best hidden-state method (≈-0.5 steps) is >30 steps\n292\t    across all models. This ''lead time wall'' at zero confirms Claim 3: hidden states\n293\t    encode current safety commitment state but not future trajectory. The finding\n294\t    is now established on both Llama-3.1 and Qwen2.5 architectures, ruling out model-specific\n295\t    artifact explanations.'\n296\t- name: TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis distance baseline\n297\t  plan_id: exp-005\n298\t  description: Estimate safe-trace covariance, compute Mahalanobis distance per step\n299\t    on all models. Evaluate as anomaly detector for commitment point.\n300\t  expected_results:\n301\t    r1_8b_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.3256\n302\t    r1_8b_mahalanobis_auroc: 0.612\n303\t    r1_32b_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.2791\n304\t    r1_32b_mahalanobis_auroc: 0.583\n305\t    qwq_32b_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.2326\n306\t    qwq_32b_mahalanobis_auroc: 0.561\n307\t    mean_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.2791\n308\t    mahalanobis_vs_temporal_gap: -0.488\n309\t  result_rationale: Mahalanobis distance 失败因为它本质上依赖 covariance structure（等价于所有 PCs\n310\t    的加权距离），而 safety signal 集中在 minor PCs（解释 <17% variance）。在 full-dimensional MD 中，major\n311\t    PCs 主导距离计算——一个步骤在 top PCs 上的偏移（反映 topic/position/syntax 变化）远大于 minor PCs 上的 safety\n312\t    signal 偏移。这导致 false positives（topic shift 被标记为 anomaly）和 false negatives（真正的 safety\n313\t    transition 在 minor PCs 上太弱）。32B 模型更差因为 5120 维空间中 minor PCs 的相对贡献更小。这直接类比了 TrajGuard\n314\t    在标准 LLM 上成功但在 reasoning model 上失败的原因：reasoning model 的 safety signal 不在 geometric\n315\t    outlier direction 上。\n316\t  tables:\n317\t  - caption: 'Table 7: Mahalanobis distance baseline vs temporal probe'\n318\t    columns:\n319\t    - Model\n320\t    - MD Coverage\n321\t    - MD AUROC\n322\t    - Temporal W15 Cov\n323\t    - Gap\n324\t    rows:\n325\t    - - r1-8b\n326\t      - 0.326\n327\t      - 0.612\n328\t      - 0.767\n329\t      - -44.1pp\n330\t    - - r1-32b\n331\t      - 0.279\n332\t      - 0.583\n333\t      - 0.791\n334\t      - -51.2pp\n335\t    - - QwQ-32B\n336\t      - 0.233\n337\t      - 0.561\n338\t      - 0.744\n339\t      - -51.1pp\n340\t  figures_description:\n341\t  - 'Figure 11: ROC curves for Mahalanobis distance vs temporal LR on all 3 models.\n342\t    MD curves barely above diagonal, temporal LR curves in upper-left region.'\n343\t  - 'Figure 12: Mahalanobis distance time series on example traces. Shows MD fluctuates\n344\t    with topic changes but doesn''t spike at commitment point, confirming geometric\n345\t    methods fail when signal is in minor PCs.'\n346\t  analysis: 'Mahalanobis baseline coverage (23-33%) is substantially below even static\n347\t    LR (40-47%), confirming that TrajGuard-style geometric anomaly detection is fundamentally\n348\t    unsuited for reasoning-model safety monitoring. The failure mode is precise and\n349\t    interpretable: safety signal lives in minor PCs that contribute negligibly to\n350\t    Mahalanobis distance. This preempts reviewer concern about comparison to existing\n351\t    detectors — they fail for principled geometric reasons, not implementation issues.'\n352\t- name: Bootstrap confidence intervals\n353\t  plan_id: exp-006\n354\t  description: 1000 bootstrap resamples on all key metrics for all methods × models.\n355\t    Report 95% CIs.\n356\t  expected_results:\n357\t    r1_8b_temporal_coverage_ci:\n358\t    - 0.674\n359\t    - 0.86\n360\t    r1_32b_temporal_coverage_ci:\n361\t    - 0.698\n362\t    - 0.884\n363\t    qwq_32b_temporal_coverage_ci:\n364\t    - 0.651\n365\t    - 0.837\n366\t    r1_8b_static_coverage_ci:\n367\t    - 0.349\n368\t    - 0.581\n369\t    r1_32b_static_coverage_ci:\n370\t    - 0.326\n371\t    - 0.558\n372\t    cross_transfer_mean_ci:\n373\t    - 0.558\n374\t    - 0.733\n375\t    lead_time_r1_8b_ci:\n376\t    - -2.8\n377\t    - 0.6\n378\t    lead_time_r1_32b_ci:\n379\t    - -3.1\n380\t    - 0.5\n381\t    delta_temporal_minus_static_ci:\n382\t    - 0.186\n383\t    - 0.512\n384\t    all_deltas_exclude_zero: true\n385\t  result_rationale: Bootstrap CIs 较宽（±9-12pp）因为测试集只有 43 traces（r1-8b）和类似规模的 32B test\n386\t    sets。但关键比较（temporal vs static delta）的 CI 不包含 0，因为 +30pp 的效应量远大于采样噪声。Coverage CI\n387\t    上界不超过 oracle ceiling（76.7%的中心点 + ~9pp = ~86% upper bound，仍合理）。Lead time CI 包含少量正值（upper\n388\t    bound ~0.5）反映了个别 traces 的 positive lead，但均值 CI 中心始终为负。209 traces 的限制是真实的——CIs\n389\t    acknowledge this honestly——但效应量足够大使得所有核心 claims 在 p<0.05 下显著。\n390\t  tables:\n391\t  - caption: 'Table 8: Bootstrap 95% confidence intervals for key metrics'\n392\t    columns:\n393\t    - Metric\n394\t    - r1-8b\n395\t    - r1-32b\n396\t    - QwQ-32B\n397\t    rows:\n398\t    - - Static Coverage\n399\t      - '[0.349, 0.581]'\n400\t      - '[0.326, 0.558]'\n401\t      - '[0.279, 0.512]'\n402\t    - - Temporal W15 Coverage\n403\t      - '[0.674, 0.860]'\n404\t      - '[0.698, 0.884]'\n405\t      - '[0.651, 0.837]'\n406\t    - - Delta (Temp-Static)\n407\t      - '[0.209, 0.488]'\n408\t      - '[0.233, 0.512]'\n409\t      - '[0.233, 0.512]'\n410\t    - - Lead Time (mean)\n411\t      - '[-2.8, 0.6]'\n412\t      - '[-3.1, 0.5]'\n413\t      - '[-2.3, 0.7]'\n414\t    - - Cross-transfer Cov\n415\t      - '[0.558, 0.733]'\n416\t      - —\n417\t      - —\n418\t  figures_description:\n419\t  - 'Figure 13: Forest plot of coverage estimates with 95% bootstrap CIs. Static and\n420\t    temporal CI ranges do not overlap for any model, confirming significant separation.'\n421\t  analysis: All core claims survive bootstrap validation. Temporal > static delta\n422\t    CIs exclude zero (minimum lower bound +18.6pp). Lead time CIs are centered negative\n423\t    with upper bounds near zero but never significantly positive. The wide CIs are\n424\t    an honest reflection of sample size — acknowledged in limitations but don't threaten\n425\t    claims because effect sizes are large relative to uncertainty.\n426\t- name: Window size ablation across architectures\n427\t  plan_id: exp-007\n428\t  description: Temporal LR with W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25 on all 3 models.\n429\t  expected_results:\n430\t    r1_8b_w1: 0.465\n431\t    r1_8b_w3: 0.535\n432\t    r1_8b_w5: 0.651\n433\t    r1_8b_w10: 0.651\n434\t    r1_8b_w15: 0.767\n435\t    r1_8b_w20: 0.767\n436\t    r1_8b_w25: 0.744\n437\t    r1_32b_w1: 0.442\n438\t    r1_32b_w5: 0.628\n439\t    r1_32b_w10: 0.698\n440\t    r1_32b_w15: 0.791\n441\t    r1_32b_w20: 0.791\n442\t    r1_32b_w25: 0.767\n443\t    qwq_32b_w1: 0.395\n444\t    qwq_32b_w5: 0.581\n445\t    qwq_32b_w10: 0.651\n446\t    qwq_32b_w15: 0.744\n447\t    qwq_32b_w20: 0.744\n448\t    qwq_32b_w25: 0.721\n449\t    optimal_w_all_models: 15\n450\t  result_rationale: W=15 是所有模型的饱和点因为 safety reasoning density decline 的时间尺度是 ~15 步——这反映了推理模型从\n451\t    safety reasoning 到 harmful execution 过渡的典型长度。W<15 时 probe 看不到完整的 decline pattern（只看到局部），W>15\n452\t    时额外 context 引入噪声（更早的步骤与 commitment 无关）且增加过拟合风险（特征维度 = W × hidden_dim 在小数据集上）。W=25\n453\t    时 coverage 轻微下降（-2-3pp）证实了过拟合假说。三个模型在同一 W 饱和证明这个时间尺度是 behavioral universal，不依赖架构。\n454\t  tables:\n455\t  - caption: 'Table 9: Coverage vs window size across architectures'\n456\t    columns:\n457\t    - W\n458\t    - r1-8b\n459\t    - r1-32b\n460\t    - QwQ-32B\n461\t    - Mean\n462\t    rows:\n463\t    - - 1\n464\t      - 0.465\n465\t      - 0.442\n466\t      - 0.395\n467\t      - 0.434\n468\t    - - 3\n469\t      - 0.535\n470\t      - 0.512\n471\t      - 0.465\n472\t      - 0.504\n473\t    - - 5\n474\t      - 0.651\n475\t      - 0.628\n476\t      - 0.581\n477\t      - 0.62\n478\t    - - 10\n479\t      - 0.651\n480\t      - 0.698\n481\t      - 0.651\n482\t      - 0.667\n483\t    - - 15\n484\t      - 0.767\n485\t      - 0.791\n486\t      - 0.744\n487\t      - 0.767\n488\t    - - 20\n489\t      - 0.767\n490\t      - 0.791\n491\t      - 0.744\n492\t      - 0.767\n493\t    - - 25\n494\t      - 0.744\n495\t      - 0.767\n496\t      - 0.721\n497\t      - 0.744\n498\t  figures_description:\n499\t  - 'Figure 14: Coverage vs window size curve for all 3 models. Shows consistent saturation\n500\t    at W=15 with slight decline at W=25. All curves have same shape shifted vertically.'\n501\t  analysis: Universal saturation at W=15 across architectures is a key finding supporting\n502\t    the 'method simplicity' narrative. The window size doesn't need architecture-specific\n503\t    tuning — the optimal temporal context is determined by the behavioral phenomenon\n504\t    (safety reasoning decline duration), not the model's internal representation.\n505\t    This directly preempts reviewer concern about hyperparameter sensitivity.\n506\t- name: Layer selection ablation on 32B models\n507\t  plan_id: exp-008\n508\t  description: Evaluate temporal probe at all layers (not just layer 14) on r1-32b\n509\t    and QwQ-32B to confirm middle-layer optimality generalizes.\n510\t  expected_results:\n511\t    r1_32b_best_layer: 22\n512\t    r1_32b_best_layer_coverage: 0.814\n513\t    r1_32b_layer_14_coverage: 0.721\n514\t    r1_32b_layer_range_good: 18-26\n515\t    qwq_32b_best_layer: 24\n516\t    qwq_32b_best_layer_coverage: 0.791\n517\t    qwq_32b_layer_14_coverage: 0.698\n518\t    qwq_32b_layer_range_good: 20-28\n519\t    relative_best_layer_r1_32b: 34% depth (layer 22/64)\n520\t    relative_best_layer_qwq_32b: 37% depth (layer 24/64)\n521\t    relative_best_layer_r1_8b: 44% depth (layer 14/32)\n522\t  result_rationale: 32B 模型有 64 层（vs r1-8b 的 32 层），最佳层在相对深度 34-37% 处（layer 22-24/64），与\n523\t    r1-8b 的 44%（layer 14/32）一致——都在 middle layers。Middle layers 最优因为：early layers encode\n524\t    低级语法特征（与 safety 无关），deep layers encode 高度 task-specific 的输出特征（过于细粒度）。Middle layers\n525\t    恰好在抽象 semantic level 上 encode safety reasoning state。绝对层数不同但相对位置一致证明这是 transformer\n526\t    depth-dependent 的 universal 现象。报告中使用 per-model best layer 结果，同时证明 default 中间层选择是\n527\t    robust 的 heuristic。\n528\t  tables:\n529\t  - caption: 'Table 10: Layer ablation (temporal W=15 coverage by layer)'\n530\t    columns:\n531\t    - Relative Depth\n532\t    - r1-8b (L/32)\n533\t    - r1-32b (L/64)\n534\t    - QwQ-32B (L/64)\n535\t    rows:\n536\t    - - 10%\n537\t      - 0.442 (L3)\n538\t      - 0.395 (L6)\n539\t      - 0.372 (L6)\n540\t    - - 25%\n541\t      - 0.605 (L8)\n542\t      - 0.581 (L16)\n543\t      - 0.558 (L16)\n544\t    - - 35%\n545\t      - 0.721 (L11)\n546\t      - 0.814 (L22)\n547\t      - 0.744 (L22)\n548\t    - - 44%\n549\t      - 0.767 (L14)\n550\t      - 0.791 (L28)\n551\t      - 0.791 (L28)\n552\t    - - 50%\n553\t      - 0.744 (L16)\n554\t      - 0.767 (L32)\n555\t      - 0.767 (L32)\n556\t    - - 75%\n557\t      - 0.628 (L24)\n558\t      - 0.651 (L48)\n559\t      - 0.628 (L48)\n560\t  figures_description:\n561\t  - 'Figure 15: Coverage vs relative layer depth (normalized 0-1) for all 3 models.\n562\t    Peak region 30-45% for all architectures, confirming middle-layer universality.'\n563\t  analysis: Middle-layer optimality generalizes to 32B models when measured in relative\n564\t    depth. The best layer at ~35-44% depth captures the 'sweet spot' between low-level\n565\t    and task-specific representations. This supports using a simple heuristic (pick\n566\t    middle third) for layer selection without architecture-specific tuning, further\n567\t    strengthening the 'simplicity' narrative.\n568\t- name: 16-label taxonomy supervision\n569\t  plan_id: exp-009\n570\t  description: Replace binary commitment label with fine-grained 16-label taxonomy\n571\t    (Type 1-4 safety labels). Train temporal probe with richer supervision signal.\n572\t  expected_results:\n573\t    r1_8b_16label_coverage: 0.791\n574\t    r1_8b_16label_lead_mean: -0.7\n575\t    r1_8b_binary_coverage: 0.767\n576\t    r1_8b_binary_lead_mean: -1.09\n577\t    r1_32b_16label_coverage: 0.814\n578\t    r1_32b_16label_lead_mean: -0.9\n579\t    improvement_over_binary: +2.4pp coverage, +0.3 lead time\n580\t    16label_accuracy_per_type:\n581\t      type1: 0.72\n582\t      type2: 0.68\n583\t      type3: 0.61\n584\t      type4: 0.54\n585\t  result_rationale: 16-label supervision 提供 marginal improvement（+2-3pp coverage）而非\n586\t    dramatic improvement 因为：(1) commitment detection 的瓶颈不是 label granularity 而是 hidden\n587\t    state 的 temporal encoding 能力——更细粒度的标签帮助 probe 学到更精确的 safety state representation，但不能突破\n588\t    hidden state 本身的信息限制；(2) 16 labels 在 209 traces 上意味着每个类别只有 ~13 traces，加剧了数据稀缺问题；(3)\n589\t    Type 3/4（更细微的 safety reasoning 类型）更难分类因为其 hidden state 表征与 Type 1/2 高度重叠。Lead\n590\t    time 略有改善因为 fine-grained labels 让 probe 能更早识别到从 Type 1→Type 4 的渐变过程。\n591\t  tables:\n592\t  - caption: 'Table 11: Binary vs 16-label supervision (temporal W=15)'\n593\t    columns:\n594\t    - Model\n595\t    - Binary Cov\n596\t    - 16-label Cov\n597\t    - Binary Lead\n598\t    - 16-label Lead\n599\t    rows:\n600\t    - - r1-8b\n601\t      - 0.767\n602\t      - 0.791\n603\t      - -1.09\n604\t      - -0.7\n605\t    - - r1-32b\n606\t      - 0.791\n607\t      - 0.814\n608\t      - -1.32\n609\t      - -0.9\n610\t  figures_description:\n611\t  - 'Figure 16: Per-type classification accuracy showing graceful degradation from\n612\t    Type 1 (clearest safety signal) to Type 4 (most subtle). Confirms that fine-grained\n613\t    safety states are partially distinguishable but with diminishing separability.'\n614\t  analysis: '16-label supervision offers marginal but not transformative improvement,\n615\t    addressing reviewer concern about underutilized supervision. The modest gains\n616\t    (+2-3pp) support rather than undermine our narrative: even with optimal supervision,\n617\t    the fundamental bottleneck is the temporal information capacity of hidden states,\n618\t    not label quality. This result goes in the ablation section as confirmatory evidence.'\n619\t- name: Oracle decomposition analysis\n620\t  plan_id: exp-010\n621\t  description: Analyze what label-sequence patterns the oracle exploits that hidden\n622\t    states cannot. Decompose oracle's +31 step advantage.\n623\t  expected_results:\n624\t    oracle_uses_streak_pattern: true\n625\t    oracle_mean_streak_before_cp: 14.6\n626\t    oracle_detects_via: consecutive safe-label absence (K=5 consecutive non-safety\n627\t      steps)\n628\t    hidden_state_encodes_current_label: true\n629\t    hidden_state_encodes_future_trajectory: false\n630\t    mutual_info_hs_current_label: 0.42\n631\t    mutual_info_hs_next5_labels: 0.08\n632\t    mutual_info_hs_next15_labels: 0.03\n633\t  result_rationale: Oracle 的优势来源于直接观察 label sequence 的 streak pattern：它在看到连续 K=5 个非\n634\t    safety 步骤时就能判定 commitment（因为在训练数据中，连续 5 步无 safety label 后恢复 safety reasoning 的概率\n635\t    <5%）。Hidden states 无法复制这个优势因为它们 encode 的是当前步的语义状态而非 future label trajectory 的统计规律。互信息分析证实：hidden\n636\t    state 与当前步 label 高度相关（MI=0.42），但与未来 5-15 步的 label 几乎无关（MI→0）。这说明 pre-textual detection\n637\t    需要的信息（future trajectory）根本不存在于当前步的 hidden state 中——这是因果性限制，不是模型能力限制。\n638\t  tables:\n639\t  - caption: 'Table 12: Mutual information between hidden states and label sequences'\n640\t    columns:\n641\t    - Target\n642\t    - MI with Hidden State\n643\t    - MI with Label History (W=15)\n644\t    rows:\n645\t    - - Current label\n646\t      - 0.42\n647\t      - 0.89\n648\t    - - Next 5 labels\n649\t      - 0.08\n650\t      - 0.31\n651\t    - - Next 15 labels\n652\t      - 0.03\n653\t      - 0.12\n654\t    - - Commitment (binary)\n655\t      - 0.15\n656\t      - 0.67\n657\t  figures_description:\n658\t  - 'Figure 17: Information decay curve — MI between hidden state at step t and labels\n659\t    at step t+k, for k=0..30. Shows rapid exponential decay, reaching floor by k≈5.\n660\t    Contrasts with label-history MI which decays slowly.'\n661\t  analysis: 'The oracle decomposition reveals that the +31 step advantage is not ''intelligence''\n662\t    but structural: label sequences are autocorrelated (safety labels cluster), so\n663\t    observing K consecutive absences is a powerful predictor of permanent absence.\n664\t    Hidden states lack this look-ahead because they encode single-step semantic state,\n665\t    not multi-step trajectory statistics. This establishes the principled impossibility\n666\t    of pre-textual detection from hidden states alone, providing theoretical grounding\n667\t    for Claim 3''s empirical finding.'\n668\t- name: OpenThinker-7B scale control\n669\t  plan_id: exp-011\n670\t  description: 4th model (Qwen2.5-7B base) for 2×2 architecture×scale matrix. Controls\n671\t    for scale confound in cross-architecture comparison.\n672\t  expected_results:\n673\t    openthinker_7b_static_coverage: 0.4186\n674\t    openthinker_7b_temporal_w15_coverage: 0.7209\n675\t    openthinker_7b_lead_mean: -1.5\n676\t    openthinker_7b_fisher_orig: 13.2\n677\t    openthinker_7b_fisher_pca3: 0.68\n678\t    scale_effect_llama: r1-8b vs (none) — N/A\n679\t    scale_effect_qwen: '7B→32B: +7pp temporal coverage'\n680\t    arch_effect_7b: 'Llama-8b (0.767) vs Qwen-7b (0.721): -4.6pp'\n681\t    arch_effect_32b: N/A (no Llama-32B)\n682\t  result_rationale: OpenThinker-7B（Qwen2.5-7B base）的表现略低于 r1-8b（Llama-8B）因为 Qwen2.5-7B\n683\t    的 hidden dimension 是 3584（vs Llama 4096），且作为较小的 Qwen 模型其 safety reasoning 能力可能略弱——表现为更短、更不一致的\n684\t    safety reasoning 序列。但关键模式仍然成立：static < 50%，temporal saturates at W=15，lead time\n685\t    negative。2×2 矩阵表明 scale 效应（+7pp from 7B→32B in Qwen family）大于 architecture 效应（-4.6pp\n686\t    Llama vs Qwen at 7-8B），但两者都远小于 method 效应（+30pp temporal vs static）。这排除了 scale\n687\t    confound 解释。\n688\t  tables:\n689\t  - caption: 'Table 13: 2×2 Architecture × Scale matrix'\n690\t    columns:\n691\t    - ''\n692\t    - 7-8B\n693\t    - 32B\n694\t    rows:\n695\t    - - Llama-3.1\n696\t      - 'r1-8b: 0.767'\n697\t      - — (not available)\n698\t    - - Qwen2.5\n699\t      - 'OpenThinker-7B: 0.721'\n700\t      - 'r1-32b: 0.791'\n701\t  figures_description:\n702\t  - 'Figure 18: Bar chart showing temporal coverage across 2×2 matrix. Method effect\n703\t    (temporal vs static) dominates over both architecture and scale effects.'\n704\t  analysis: The 2×2 matrix demonstrates that temporal advantage is robust to both\n705\t    architecture and scale variations. Scale provides modest improvement (+7pp within\n706\t    Qwen family) but the fundamental pattern (static fails, temporal saturates, lead\n707\t    time negative) holds at both scales. This controls for the confound that 32B models\n708\t    might simply be 'easier to probe' due to richer representations.\n709\t- name: GRU/Attention probe upper bound on 32B models\n710\t  plan_id: exp-012\n711\t  description: Train GRU probe on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Verify that complex architectures\n712\t    still don't outperform temporal LR at current data scale.\n713\t  expected_results:\n714\t    r1_32b_gru_coverage: 0.7674\n715\t    r1_32b_gru_acc: 0.8421\n716\t    r1_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.6\n717\t    r1_32b_lr_temporal_coverage: 0.7907\n718\t    r1_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: -0.023\n719\t    qwq_32b_gru_coverage: 0.7209\n720\t    qwq_32b_gru_acc: 0.8312\n721\t    qwq_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.4\n722\t    qwq_32b_lr_temporal_coverage: 0.7442\n723\t    qwq_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: -0.023\n724\t    gru_overfitting_rate: 0.35\n725\t  result_rationale: GRU 在 32B 模型上不优于（甚至略低于）temporal LR 因为：(1) 209 traces × ~50 steps/trace\n726\t    的训练数据不足以让 1.6M 参数的 GRU 学到 LR 不能捕捉的非线性模式——GRU 的额外容量只增加了过拟合风险；(2) safety reasoning\n727\t    density decline 本身是近似线性的时序模式（密度从高到低单调递减），LR 足以捕捉；(3) r1-8b 上已观察到 GRU coverage\n728\t    (0.674) < temporal LR (0.767)，32B 模型上 gap 更小（-2.3pp）因为 5120-dim hidden states\n729\t    给 GRU 更多信息，但仍不足以超越 LR 在小数据上的 regularization 优势。Lead time 略好于 LR（-0.4~-0.6 vs -0.87~-1.32）但仍为负，证明\n730\t    architecture complexity 不能解决 fundamental lead time limitation。\n731\t  tables:\n732\t  - caption: 'Table 14: GRU vs Temporal LR on 32B models'\n733\t    columns:\n734\t    - Model\n735\t    - Method\n736\t    - Coverage\n737\t    - Accuracy\n738\t    - Lead Mean\n739\t    - Params\n740\t    rows:\n741\t    - - r1-32b\n742\t      - Temporal LR W=15\n743\t      - 0.791\n744\t      - 0.851\n745\t      - -1.32\n746\t      - 76.8K\n747\t    - - r1-32b\n748\t      - GRU-256\n749\t      - 0.767\n750\t      - 0.842\n751\t      - -0.6\n752\t      - 1.62M\n753\t    - - QwQ-32B\n754\t      - Temporal LR W=15\n755\t      - 0.744\n756\t      - 0.839\n757\t      - -0.87\n758\t      - 76.8K\n759\t    - - QwQ-32B\n760\t      - GRU-256\n761\t      - 0.721\n762\t      - 0.831\n763\t      - -0.4\n764\t      - 1.62M\n765\t  figures_description:\n766\t  - 'Figure 19: Learning curves (train vs val loss) for GRU on 32B models. Shows overfitting\n767\t    onset at epoch 8-10, confirming data insufficiency. LR does not exhibit this behavior.'\n768\t  analysis: 'GRU''s failure to improve over temporal LR on 32B models (actually -2.3pp)\n769\t    definitively supports the ''simplicity is optimal'' narrative. At current data\n770\t    scales (209 traces), the additional model complexity of GRU (21× more parameters)\n771\t    only increases overfitting. This finding is strengthened by being replicated across\n772\t    architectures: it''s not that GRU fails on a specific model, but that the data\n773\t    regime makes complex temporal models counterproductive. This directly preempts\n774\t    reviewer concern #1 about method novelty — simplicity isn''t a limitation, it''s\n775\t    the correct choice given the data-method trade-off.'\n776\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f13d24b-577b-4045-a090-ff893be7f4fd","uuid":"1b4ef17c-59bf-489b-ae2d-3107aee9a2a2","timestamp":"2026-05-16T20:09:52.218Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T194646/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: Original 3-claim structure holds at full strength. Frame as first\n  cross-architecture empirical study establishing universal properties of hidden-state\n  safety monitoring in reasoning models. Method simplicity is the finding (reviewer\n  concern 1 preempted). Negative lead time is a principled boundary result. EMNLP\n  Main with high confidence.\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Cross-architecture static probe evaluation\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: Train static LR on r1-32b and QwQ-32B hidden states, measure per-step\n    classification accuracy and detection coverage.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_static_acc: 0.8243\n    r1_32b_static_coverage: 0.4419\n    r1_32b_fisher_orig_L14: 16.3\n    r1_32b_fisher_orig_L20: 17.1\n    r1_32b_fisher_pca3_L14: 0.87\n    r1_32b_var_explained_3pc: 0.142\n    qwq_32b_static_acc: 0.8091\n    qwq_32b_static_coverage: 0.3953\n    qwq_32b_fisher_orig_L14: 14.8\n    qwq_32b_fisher_orig_L20: 15.6\n    qwq_32b_fisher_pca3_L14: 0.72\n    qwq_32b_var_explained_3pc: 0.128\n    mean_cross_arch_static_coverage: 0.4186\n  result_rationale: Qwen2.5 架构使用 GQA 且 hidden dimension 为 5120（vs Llama-3.1 的 4096），导致\n    safety signal 分布在更多维度上。Fisher 判别比在原始空间仍然很高（14-17），证明 safety signal 存在但同样集中在 minor\n    PCs——PCA top-3 解释方差更低（12-14% vs 16.6%），因为 5120 维空间中信号散布更广。静态 LR 仍能达到 ~81% accuracy（因为\n    majority class baseline 高），但 coverage 低于 50% 因为单步分类无法捕捉 safety reasoning density\n    decline 的渐变模式。QwQ-32B 略低于 r1-32b 因为其推理链更长更多样，commitment boundary 更模糊。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 3: Static probe performance across architectures'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Base Arch\n    - Hidden Dim\n    - Static Acc\n    - Static Coverage\n    - Fisher (orig)\n    - Fisher (PCA-3)\n    - Var Explained (3PC)\n    rows:\n    - - r1-8b\n      - Llama-3.1\n      - 4096\n      - 0.8172\n      - 0.4651\n      - 17.88\n      - 0.928\n      - 0.166\n    - - r1-32b\n      - Qwen2.5\n      - 5120\n      - 0.8243\n      - 0.4419\n      - 17.1\n      - 0.87\n      - 0.142\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - Qwen2.5\n      - 5120\n      - 0.8091\n      - 0.3953\n      - 15.6\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.128\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: Fisher discriminant ratio vs PCA dimensionality for all 3 models. Shows\n    consistent collapse from 15-18 (full space) to <1.5 (PCA-3) across architectures,\n    confirming signal-in-minor-PCs is universal.'\n  - 'Figure 5: PCA-3D scatter of safe vs unsafe steps for r1-32b and QwQ-32B (analogous\n    to Figure 2 from r1-8b). Both show overlapping clusters confirming geometric separation\n    fails in low-D projection.'\n  analysis: 'Static probe failure replicates perfectly: all models show coverage <50%\n    despite high-dimensional Fisher ratios >14. The pattern is architecture-independent\n    — safety signal exists in hidden states but is distributed across minor principal\n    components in both Llama and Qwen2.5 backbones. This directly validates Claim\n    1 as an architectural universal.'\n- name: Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: Train temporal LR W=15 on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Validate +25-35pp coverage\n    improvement holds cross-architecture.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_temporal_w15_acc: 0.8512\n    r1_32b_temporal_w15_coverage: 0.7907\n    r1_32b_temporal_minus_static_delta: 0.3488\n    r1_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -1.32\n    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_acc: 0.8389\n    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_coverage: 0.7442\n    qwq_32b_temporal_minus_static_delta: 0.3489\n    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -0.87\n    mean_cross_arch_temporal_coverage: 0.7674\n    mean_cross_arch_delta: 0.3489\n  result_rationale: Temporal window 捕捉的是 safety reasoning density decline 模式——连续 15\n    步内 safety-labeled 步骤的密度从高到低的趋势。这个模式是推理模型 self-jailbreak 的固有特征：模型先进行 safety reasoning，然后逐渐过渡到\n    harmful execution。无论底层架构是 Llama 还是 Qwen2.5，这个 behavioral pattern 都会被 encoded 进\n    hidden states 的时序轨迹中。r1-32b 略高于 QwQ 因为 DeepSeek 蒸馏对齐更干净，commitment boundary 更\n    sharp；QwQ 的推理链更长更弯曲但仍然满足 saturation。Delta 在两个模型上都 ~35pp 因为 static baseline 和 temporal\n    ceiling 的 gap 反映的是同一个结构性限制。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 4: Temporal window probe performance across architectures'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Static Cov\n    - Temporal W15 Cov\n    - Delta\n    - Temporal Acc\n    - Lead Time (mean)\n    rows:\n    - - r1-8b\n      - 0.4651\n      - 0.7674\n      - +30.2pp\n      - 0.8478\n      - -1.09\n    - - r1-32b\n      - 0.4419\n      - 0.7907\n      - +34.9pp\n      - 0.8512\n      - -1.32\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - 0.3953\n      - 0.7442\n      - +34.9pp\n      - 0.8389\n      - -0.87\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 6: Coverage vs window size W for all 3 models (W=1,5,10,15,20). Shows\n    consistent saturation at W≈15 across architectures, with diminishing returns beyond.'\n  - 'Figure 7: Per-trace detection timeline comparison (static vs temporal W=15) on\n    representative QwQ-32B traces. Shows temporal probe crossing commitment boundary\n    while static probe misses.'\n  analysis: Temporal advantage replicates with even larger delta on Qwen2.5 models\n    (+34.9pp vs +30.2pp on r1-8b). This is because Qwen2.5-based models have slightly\n    lower static baselines (due to more distributed signal) but temporal probes still\n    saturate near oracle ceiling. The consistency of saturation at W=15 across architectures\n    confirms that safety reasoning density decline operates at a universal timescale\n    (~15 reasoning steps). Claim 2 is fully validated cross-architecture.\n- name: Cross-model transfer with projection head\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: Train probe on r1-8b (Llama, 4096-dim), test on r1-32b/QwQ (Qwen2.5,\n    5120-dim) via learned linear projection. Bidirectional transfer.\n  expected_results:\n    llama_to_qwen_r1_32b_coverage: 0.6279\n    llama_to_qwen_qwq_coverage: 0.5814\n    qwen_to_llama_r1_8b_coverage: 0.6512\n    qwen_r1_32b_to_qwq_coverage: 0.7209\n    mean_cross_transfer_coverage: 0.6454\n    projection_head_params: 20971520\n    projection_training_traces: 30\n  result_rationale: Cross-transfer 成功（coverage 0.55-0.72）因为 safety signal 的时序结构是 universal\n    的——density decline pattern 在投影后仍可识别。Llama→Qwen 方向略低于 Qwen→Llama 因为 4096→5120 投影是升维（信息无损），而\n    5120→4096 是降维但 safety signal 主要在 minor PCs 所以投影头学到了保留关键维度。同族模型间转移（r1-32b→QwQ，都是\n    Qwen2.5）效果最好（0.72）因为不需要跨架构投影，只需对齐同架构的不同微调变体。Zero-shot 不达到 in-distribution 水平（0.77）是因为不同模型的\n    commitment 边界位置和 hidden state 表征存在分布偏移，但 >55% 证明 safety monitoring 有跨架构泛化潜力。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 5: Cross-architecture transfer matrix (temporal W=15 coverage)'\n    columns:\n    - Train →\n    - 'Test: r1-8b'\n    - 'Test: r1-32b'\n    - 'Test: QwQ-32B'\n    rows:\n    - - r1-8b (Llama)\n      - 0.767 (in-dist)\n      - '0.628'\n      - '0.581'\n    - - r1-32b (Qwen2.5)\n      - '0.651'\n      - 0.791 (in-dist)\n      - '0.721'\n    - - QwQ-32B (Qwen2.5)\n      - '0.605'\n      - '0.698'\n      - 0.744 (in-dist)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 8: Transfer matrix heatmap showing coverage degradation from in-distribution\n    (diagonal) to cross-architecture (off-diagonal). Intra-family transfer (Qwen↔Qwen)\n    degrades less than cross-family (Llama↔Qwen).'\n  analysis: Non-trivial cross-architecture transfer (mean 0.645) demonstrates that\n    safety commitment signal has a shared geometric structure across model families.\n    The projection head successfully maps between representation spaces while preserving\n    the temporal density decline pattern. This is the strongest evidence for 'architectural\n    universal' framing — a probe trained on one model family can monitor another with\n    >55% coverage without any target-domain labels.\n- name: Lead time analysis across architectures\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: Measure detection lead time (steps before/after textual commitment\n    point) for all methods on r1-32b and QwQ-32B.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_static_lead_mean: -2.8\n    r1_32b_static_lead_median: -3\n    r1_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -1.32\n    r1_32b_temporal_w15_lead_median: -1\n    r1_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.9\n    r1_32b_positive_lead_rate: 0.29\n    qwq_32b_static_lead_mean: -1.9\n    qwq_32b_static_lead_median: -2\n    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_lead_mean: -0.87\n    qwq_32b_temporal_w15_lead_median: -1\n    qwq_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.5\n    qwq_32b_positive_lead_rate: 0.33\n    all_models_max_lead_mean: -0.2\n    oracle_lead_mean: 31\n  result_rationale: Negative lead time 在所有模型上持续出现因为这反映了一个根本性限制：hidden states encode\n    当前 safety state 而非未来 safety trajectory。模型在 commitment point 处才在 hidden space 中完成从\n    safety→unsafe 的转变——这个转变是 concurrent with（而非 prior to）文本层面的 commitment。Oracle 能提前\n    31 步检测是因为它直接观察 label sequence 中的 density decline pattern（这是定义层面的优势，不依赖 hidden\n    representation）。QwQ 的 lead time 略好于 r1-32b（-0.87 vs -1.32）因为 QwQ 的推理链更长，commitment\n    boundary 更 gradual，给 temporal probe 更多 context 来识别过渡区。但无论哪个模型，mean lead time 都不超过\n    0，确认 pre-textual detection limitation 是 fundamental 的。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 6: Detection lead time across architectures (steps relative to\n      commitment point)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Method\n    - Lead Mean\n    - Lead Median\n    - Positive Lead %\n    - Coverage\n    rows:\n    - - r1-8b\n      - Static LR\n      - -2.0\n      - -2\n      - 30%\n      - 0.465\n    - - r1-8b\n      - Temporal W15\n      - -1.09\n      - -1\n      - 34%\n      - 0.767\n    - - r1-8b\n      - GRU\n      - -0.21\n      - -1\n      - 34.5%\n      - 0.674\n    - - r1-32b\n      - Static LR\n      - -2.8\n      - -3\n      - 25%\n      - 0.442\n    - - r1-32b\n      - Temporal W15\n      - -1.32\n      - -1\n      - 29%\n      - 0.791\n    - - r1-32b\n      - GRU\n      - -0.9\n      - -1\n      - 29%\n      - 0.721\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - Static LR\n      - -1.9\n      - -2\n      - 28%\n      - 0.395\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - Temporal W15\n      - -0.87\n      - -1\n      - 33%\n      - 0.744\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - GRU\n      - -0.5\n      - 0\n      - 33%\n      - 0.698\n    - - All\n      - Oracle (K=5)\n      - 31\n      - 29\n      - 100%\n      - 1.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 9: Lead time distribution (violin plot) across 3 models × 3 methods. All\n    method distributions centered at or below 0; oracle distribution centered at +31.\n    Clear separation between hidden-state methods and label-oracle.'\n  - 'Figure 10: Lead time vs coverage scatter for all model×method combinations. Shows\n    Pareto frontier: higher coverage methods have slightly less negative lead time,\n    but none cross zero mean.'\n  analysis: 'Negative lead time is confirmed as architecture-independent. The gap\n    between oracle (+31 steps) and best hidden-state method (≈-0.5 steps) is >30 steps\n    across all models. This ''lead time wall'' at zero confirms Claim 3: hidden states\n    encode current safety commitment state but not future trajectory. The finding\n    is now established on both Llama-3.1 and Qwen2.5 architectures, ruling out model-specific\n    artifact explanations.'\n- name: TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis distance baseline\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: Estimate safe-trace covariance, compute Mahalanobis distance per step\n    on all models. Evaluate as anomaly detector for commitment point.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.3256\n    r1_8b_mahalanobis_auroc: 0.612\n    r1_32b_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.2791\n    r1_32b_mahalanobis_auroc: 0.583\n    qwq_32b_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.2326\n    qwq_32b_mahalanobis_auroc: 0.561\n    mean_mahalanobis_coverage: 0.2791\n    mahalanobis_vs_temporal_gap: -0.488\n  result_rationale: Mahalanobis distance 失败因为它本质上依赖 covariance structure（等价于所有 PCs\n    的加权距离），而 safety signal 集中在 minor PCs（解释 <17% variance）。在 full-dimensional MD 中，major\n    PCs 主导距离计算——一个步骤在 top PCs 上的偏移（反映 topic/position/syntax 变化）远大于 minor PCs 上的 safety\n    signal 偏移。这导致 false positives（topic shift 被标记为 anomaly）和 false negatives（真正的 safety\n    transition 在 minor PCs 上太弱）。32B 模型更差因为 5120 维空间中 minor PCs 的相对贡献更小。这直接类比了 TrajGuard\n    在标准 LLM 上成功但在 reasoning model 上失败的原因：reasoning model 的 safety signal 不在 geometric\n    outlier direction 上。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 7: Mahalanobis distance baseline vs temporal probe'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - MD Coverage\n    - MD AUROC\n    - Temporal W15 Cov\n    - Gap\n    rows:\n    - - r1-8b\n      - 0.326\n      - 0.612\n      - 0.767\n      - -44.1pp\n    - - r1-32b\n      - 0.279\n      - 0.583\n      - 0.791\n      - -51.2pp\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - 0.233\n      - 0.561\n      - 0.744\n      - -51.1pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 11: ROC curves for Mahalanobis distance vs temporal LR on all 3 models.\n    MD curves barely above diagonal, temporal LR curves in upper-left region.'\n  - 'Figure 12: Mahalanobis distance time series on example traces. Shows MD fluctuates\n    with topic changes but doesn''t spike at commitment point, confirming geometric\n    methods fail when signal is in minor PCs.'\n  analysis: 'Mahalanobis baseline coverage (23-33%) is substantially below even static\n    LR (40-47%), confirming that TrajGuard-style geometric anomaly detection is fundamentally\n    unsuited for reasoning-model safety monitoring. The failure mode is precise and\n    interpretable: safety signal lives in minor PCs that contribute negligibly to\n    Mahalanobis distance. This preempts reviewer concern about comparison to existing\n    detectors — they fail for principled geometric reasons, not implementation issues.'\n- name: Bootstrap confidence intervals\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 1000 bootstrap resamples on all key metrics for all methods × models.\n    Report 95% CIs.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_temporal_coverage_ci:\n    - 0.674\n    - 0.86\n    r1_32b_temporal_coverage_ci:\n    - 0.698\n    - 0.884\n    qwq_32b_temporal_coverage_ci:\n    - 0.651\n    - 0.837\n    r1_8b_static_coverage_ci:\n    - 0.349\n    - 0.581\n    r1_32b_static_coverage_ci:\n    - 0.326\n    - 0.558\n    cross_transfer_mean_ci:\n    - 0.558\n    - 0.733\n    lead_time_r1_8b_ci:\n    - -2.8\n    - 0.6\n    lead_time_r1_32b_ci:\n    - -3.1\n    - 0.5\n    delta_temporal_minus_static_ci:\n    - 0.186\n    - 0.512\n    all_deltas_exclude_zero: true\n  result_rationale: Bootstrap CIs 较宽（±9-12pp）因为测试集只有 43 traces（r1-8b）和类似规模的 32B test\n    sets。但关键比较（temporal vs static delta）的 CI 不包含 0，因为 +30pp 的效应量远大于采样噪声。Coverage CI\n    上界不超过 oracle ceiling（76.7%的中心点 + ~9pp = ~86% upper bound，仍合理）。Lead time CI 包含少量正值（upper\n    bound ~0.5）反映了个别 traces 的 positive lead，但均值 CI 中心始终为负。209 traces 的限制是真实的——CIs\n    acknowledge this honestly——但效应量足够大使得所有核心 claims 在 p<0.05 下显著。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 8: Bootstrap 95% confidence intervals for key metrics'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - r1-8b\n    - r1-32b\n    - QwQ-32B\n    rows:\n    - - Static Coverage\n      - '[0.349, 0.581]'\n      - '[0.326, 0.558]'\n      - '[0.279, 0.512]'\n    - - Temporal W15 Coverage\n      - '[0.674, 0.860]'\n      - '[0.698, 0.884]'\n      - '[0.651, 0.837]'\n    - - Delta (Temp-Static)\n      - '[0.209, 0.488]'\n      - '[0.233, 0.512]'\n      - '[0.233, 0.512]'\n    - - Lead Time (mean)\n      - '[-2.8, 0.6]'\n      - '[-3.1, 0.5]'\n      - '[-2.3, 0.7]'\n    - - Cross-transfer Cov\n      - '[0.558, 0.733]'\n      - —\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 13: Forest plot of coverage estimates with 95% bootstrap CIs. Static and\n    temporal CI ranges do not overlap for any model, confirming significant separation.'\n  analysis: All core claims survive bootstrap validation. Temporal > static delta\n    CIs exclude zero (minimum lower bound +18.6pp). Lead time CIs are centered negative\n    with upper bounds near zero but never significantly positive. The wide CIs are\n    an honest reflection of sample size — acknowledged in limitations but don't threaten\n    claims because effect sizes are large relative to uncertainty.\n- name: Window size ablation across architectures\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: Temporal LR with W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25 on all 3 models.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_w1: 0.465\n    r1_8b_w3: 0.535\n    r1_8b_w5: 0.651\n    r1_8b_w10: 0.651\n    r1_8b_w15: 0.767\n    r1_8b_w20: 0.767\n    r1_8b_w25: 0.744\n    r1_32b_w1: 0.442\n    r1_32b_w5: 0.628\n    r1_32b_w10: 0.698\n    r1_32b_w15: 0.791\n    r1_32b_w20: 0.791\n    r1_32b_w25: 0.767\n    qwq_32b_w1: 0.395\n    qwq_32b_w5: 0.581\n    qwq_32b_w10: 0.651\n    qwq_32b_w15: 0.744\n    qwq_32b_w20: 0.744\n    qwq_32b_w25: 0.721\n    optimal_w_all_models: 15\n  result_rationale: W=15 是所有模型的饱和点因为 safety reasoning density decline 的时间尺度是 ~15 步——这反映了推理模型从\n    safety reasoning 到 harmful execution 过渡的典型长度。W<15 时 probe 看不到完整的 decline pattern（只看到局部），W>15\n    时额外 context 引入噪声（更早的步骤与 commitment 无关）且增加过拟合风险（特征维度 = W × hidden_dim 在小数据集上）。W=25\n    时 coverage 轻微下降（-2-3pp）证实了过拟合假说。三个模型在同一 W 饱和证明这个时间尺度是 behavioral universal，不依赖架构。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 9: Coverage vs window size across architectures'\n    columns:\n    - W\n    - r1-8b\n    - r1-32b\n    - QwQ-32B\n    - Mean\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.465\n      - 0.442\n      - 0.395\n      - 0.434\n    - - 3\n      - 0.535\n      - 0.512\n      - 0.465\n      - 0.504\n    - - 5\n      - 0.651\n      - 0.628\n      - 0.581\n      - 0.62\n    - - 10\n      - 0.651\n      - 0.698\n      - 0.651\n      - 0.667\n    - - 15\n      - 0.767\n      - 0.791\n      - 0.744\n      - 0.767\n    - - 20\n      - 0.767\n      - 0.791\n      - 0.744\n      - 0.767\n    - - 25\n      - 0.744\n      - 0.767\n      - 0.721\n      - 0.744\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 14: Coverage vs window size curve for all 3 models. Shows consistent saturation\n    at W=15 with slight decline at W=25. All curves have same shape shifted vertically.'\n  analysis: Universal saturation at W=15 across architectures is a key finding supporting\n    the 'method simplicity' narrative. The window size doesn't need architecture-specific\n    tuning — the optimal temporal context is determined by the behavioral phenomenon\n    (safety reasoning decline duration), not the model's internal representation.\n    This directly preempts reviewer concern about hyperparameter sensitivity.\n- name: Layer selection ablation on 32B models\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: Evaluate temporal probe at all layers (not just layer 14) on r1-32b\n    and QwQ-32B to confirm middle-layer optimality generalizes.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_best_layer: 22\n    r1_32b_best_layer_coverage: 0.814\n    r1_32b_layer_14_coverage: 0.721\n    r1_32b_layer_range_good: 18-26\n    qwq_32b_best_layer: 24\n    qwq_32b_best_layer_coverage: 0.791\n    qwq_32b_layer_14_coverage: 0.698\n    qwq_32b_layer_range_good: 20-28\n    relative_best_layer_r1_32b: 34% depth (layer 22/64)\n    relative_best_layer_qwq_32b: 37% depth (layer 24/64)\n    relative_best_layer_r1_8b: 44% depth (layer 14/32)\n  result_rationale: 32B 模型有 64 层（vs r1-8b 的 32 层），最佳层在相对深度 34-37% 处（layer 22-24/64），与\n    r1-8b 的 44%（layer 14/32）一致——都在 middle layers。Middle layers 最优因为：early layers encode\n    低级语法特征（与 safety 无关），deep layers encode 高度 task-specific 的输出特征（过于细粒度）。Middle layers\n    恰好在抽象 semantic level 上 encode safety reasoning state。绝对层数不同但相对位置一致证明这是 transformer\n    depth-dependent 的 universal 现象。报告中使用 per-model best layer 结果，同时证明 default 中间层选择是\n    robust 的 heuristic。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 10: Layer ablation (temporal W=15 coverage by layer)'\n    columns:\n    - Relative Depth\n    - r1-8b (L/32)\n    - r1-32b (L/64)\n    - QwQ-32B (L/64)\n    rows:\n    - - 10%\n      - 0.442 (L3)\n      - 0.395 (L6)\n      - 0.372 (L6)\n    - - 25%\n      - 0.605 (L8)\n      - 0.581 (L16)\n      - 0.558 (L16)\n    - - 35%\n      - 0.721 (L11)\n      - 0.814 (L22)\n      - 0.744 (L22)\n    - - 44%\n      - 0.767 (L14)\n      - 0.791 (L28)\n      - 0.791 (L28)\n    - - 50%\n      - 0.744 (L16)\n      - 0.767 (L32)\n      - 0.767 (L32)\n    - - 75%\n      - 0.628 (L24)\n      - 0.651 (L48)\n      - 0.628 (L48)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 15: Coverage vs relative layer depth (normalized 0-1) for all 3 models.\n    Peak region 30-45% for all architectures, confirming middle-layer universality.'\n  analysis: Middle-layer optimality generalizes to 32B models when measured in relative\n    depth. The best layer at ~35-44% depth captures the 'sweet spot' between low-level\n    and task-specific representations. This supports using a simple heuristic (pick\n    middle third) for layer selection without architecture-specific tuning, further\n    strengthening the 'simplicity' narrative.\n- name: 16-label taxonomy supervision\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: Replace binary commitment label with fine-grained 16-label taxonomy\n    (Type 1-4 safety labels). Train temporal probe with richer supervision signal.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_16label_coverage: 0.791\n    r1_8b_16label_lead_mean: -0.7\n    r1_8b_binary_coverage: 0.767\n    r1_8b_binary_lead_mean: -1.09\n    r1_32b_16label_coverage: 0.814\n    r1_32b_16label_lead_mean: -0.9\n    improvement_over_binary: +2.4pp coverage, +0.3 lead time\n    16label_accuracy_per_type:\n      type1: 0.72\n      type2: 0.68\n      type3: 0.61\n      type4: 0.54\n  result_rationale: 16-label supervision 提供 marginal improvement（+2-3pp coverage）而非\n    dramatic improvement 因为：(1) commitment detection 的瓶颈不是 label granularity 而是 hidden\n    state 的 temporal encoding 能力——更细粒度的标签帮助 probe 学到更精确的 safety state representation，但不能突破\n    hidden state 本身的信息限制；(2) 16 labels 在 209 traces 上意味着每个类别只有 ~13 traces，加剧了数据稀缺问题；(3)\n    Type 3/4（更细微的 safety reasoning 类型）更难分类因为其 hidden state 表征与 Type 1/2 高度重叠。Lead\n    time 略有改善因为 fine-grained labels 让 probe 能更早识别到从 Type 1→Type 4 的渐变过程。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 11: Binary vs 16-label supervision (temporal W=15)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Binary Cov\n    - 16-label Cov\n    - Binary Lead\n    - 16-label Lead\n    rows:\n    - - r1-8b\n      - 0.767\n      - 0.791\n      - -1.09\n      - -0.7\n    - - r1-32b\n      - 0.791\n      - 0.814\n      - -1.32\n      - -0.9\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 16: Per-type classification accuracy showing graceful degradation from\n    Type 1 (clearest safety signal) to Type 4 (most subtle). Confirms that fine-grained\n    safety states are partially distinguishable but with diminishing separability.'\n  analysis: '16-label supervision offers marginal but not transformative improvement,\n    addressing reviewer concern about underutilized supervision. The modest gains\n    (+2-3pp) support rather than undermine our narrative: even with optimal supervision,\n    the fundamental bottleneck is the temporal information capacity of hidden states,\n    not label quality. This result goes in the ablation section as confirmatory evidence.'\n- name: Oracle decomposition analysis\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: Analyze what label-sequence patterns the oracle exploits that hidden\n    states cannot. Decompose oracle's +31 step advantage.\n  expected_results:\n    oracle_uses_streak_pattern: true\n    oracle_mean_streak_before_cp: 14.6\n    oracle_detects_via: consecutive safe-label absence (K=5 consecutive non-safety\n      steps)\n    hidden_state_encodes_current_label: true\n    hidden_state_encodes_future_trajectory: false\n    mutual_info_hs_current_label: 0.42\n    mutual_info_hs_next5_labels: 0.08\n    mutual_info_hs_next15_labels: 0.03\n  result_rationale: Oracle 的优势来源于直接观察 label sequence 的 streak pattern：它在看到连续 K=5 个非\n    safety 步骤时就能判定 commitment（因为在训练数据中，连续 5 步无 safety label 后恢复 safety reasoning 的概率\n    <5%）。Hidden states 无法复制这个优势因为它们 encode 的是当前步的语义状态而非 future label trajectory 的统计规律。互信息分析证实：hidden\n    state 与当前步 label 高度相关（MI=0.42），但与未来 5-15 步的 label 几乎无关（MI→0）。这说明 pre-textual detection\n    需要的信息（future trajectory）根本不存在于当前步的 hidden state 中——这是因果性限制，不是模型能力限制。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 12: Mutual information between hidden states and label sequences'\n    columns:\n    - Target\n    - MI with Hidden State\n    - MI with Label History (W=15)\n    rows:\n    - - Current label\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.89\n    - - Next 5 labels\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.31\n    - - Next 15 labels\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.12\n    - - Commitment (binary)\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.67\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 17: Information decay curve — MI between hidden state at step t and labels\n    at step t+k, for k=0..30. Shows rapid exponential decay, reaching floor by k≈5.\n    Contrasts with label-history MI which decays slowly.'\n  analysis: 'The oracle decomposition reveals that the +31 step advantage is not ''intelligence''\n    but structural: label sequences are autocorrelated (safety labels cluster), so\n    observing K consecutive absences is a powerful predictor of permanent absence.\n    Hidden states lack this look-ahead because they encode single-step semantic state,\n    not multi-step trajectory statistics. This establishes the principled impossibility\n    of pre-textual detection from hidden states alone, providing theoretical grounding\n    for Claim 3''s empirical finding.'\n- name: OpenThinker-7B scale control\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 4th model (Qwen2.5-7B base) for 2×2 architecture×scale matrix. Controls\n    for scale confound in cross-architecture comparison.\n  expected_results:\n    openthinker_7b_static_coverage: 0.4186\n    openthinker_7b_temporal_w15_coverage: 0.7209\n    openthinker_7b_lead_mean: -1.5\n    openthinker_7b_fisher_orig: 13.2\n    openthinker_7b_fisher_pca3: 0.68\n    scale_effect_llama: r1-8b vs (none) — N/A\n    scale_effect_qwen: '7B→32B: +7pp temporal coverage'\n    arch_effect_7b: 'Llama-8b (0.767) vs Qwen-7b (0.721): -4.6pp'\n    arch_effect_32b: N/A (no Llama-32B)\n  result_rationale: OpenThinker-7B（Qwen2.5-7B base）的表现略低于 r1-8b（Llama-8B）因为 Qwen2.5-7B\n    的 hidden dimension 是 3584（vs Llama 4096），且作为较小的 Qwen 模型其 safety reasoning 能力可能略弱——表现为更短、更不一致的\n    safety reasoning 序列。但关键模式仍然成立：static < 50%，temporal saturates at W=15，lead time\n    negative。2×2 矩阵表明 scale 效应（+7pp from 7B→32B in Qwen family）大于 architecture 效应（-4.6pp\n    Llama vs Qwen at 7-8B），但两者都远小于 method 效应（+30pp temporal vs static）。这排除了 scale\n    confound 解释。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 13: 2×2 Architecture × Scale matrix'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - 7-8B\n    - 32B\n    rows:\n    - - Llama-3.1\n      - 'r1-8b: 0.767'\n      - — (not available)\n    - - Qwen2.5\n      - 'OpenThinker-7B: 0.721'\n      - 'r1-32b: 0.791'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 18: Bar chart showing temporal coverage across 2×2 matrix. Method effect\n    (temporal vs static) dominates over both architecture and scale effects.'\n  analysis: The 2×2 matrix demonstrates that temporal advantage is robust to both\n    architecture and scale variations. Scale provides modest improvement (+7pp within\n    Qwen family) but the fundamental pattern (static fails, temporal saturates, lead\n    time negative) holds at both scales. This controls for the confound that 32B models\n    might simply be 'easier to probe' due to richer representations.\n- name: GRU/Attention probe upper bound on 32B models\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: Train GRU probe on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Verify that complex architectures\n    still don't outperform temporal LR at current data scale.\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_gru_coverage: 0.7674\n    r1_32b_gru_acc: 0.8421\n    r1_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.6\n    r1_32b_lr_temporal_coverage: 0.7907\n    r1_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: -0.023\n    qwq_32b_gru_coverage: 0.7209\n    qwq_32b_gru_acc: 0.8312\n    qwq_32b_gru_lead_mean: -0.4\n    qwq_32b_lr_temporal_coverage: 0.7442\n    qwq_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: -0.023\n    gru_overfitting_rate: 0.35\n  result_rationale: GRU 在 32B 模型上不优于（甚至略低于）temporal LR 因为：(1) 209 traces × ~50 steps/trace\n    的训练数据不足以让 1.6M 参数的 GRU 学到 LR 不能捕捉的非线性模式——GRU 的额外容量只增加了过拟合风险；(2) safety reasoning\n    density decline 本身是近似线性的时序模式（密度从高到低单调递减），LR 足以捕捉；(3) r1-8b 上已观察到 GRU coverage\n    (0.674) < temporal LR (0.767)，32B 模型上 gap 更小（-2.3pp）因为 5120-dim hidden states\n    给 GRU 更多信息，但仍不足以超越 LR 在小数据上的 regularization 优势。Lead time 略好于 LR（-0.4~-0.6 vs -0.87~-1.32）但仍为负，证明\n    architecture complexity 不能解决 fundamental lead time limitation。\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Table 14: GRU vs Temporal LR on 32B models'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Method\n    - Coverage\n    - Accuracy\n    - Lead Mean\n    - Params\n    rows:\n    - - r1-32b\n      - Temporal LR W=15\n      - 0.791\n      - 0.851\n      - -1.32\n      - 76.8K\n    - - r1-32b\n      - GRU-256\n      - 0.767\n      - 0.842\n      - -0.6\n      - 1.62M\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - Temporal LR W=15\n      - 0.744\n      - 0.839\n      - -0.87\n      - 76.8K\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - GRU-256\n      - 0.721\n      - 0.831\n      - -0.4\n      - 1.62M\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 19: Learning curves (train vs val loss) for GRU on 32B models. Shows overfitting\n    onset at epoch 8-10, confirming data insufficiency. LR does not exhibit this behavior.'\n  analysis: 'GRU''s failure to improve over temporal LR on 32B models (actually -2.3pp)\n    definitively supports the ''simplicity is optimal'' narrative. At current data\n    scales (209 traces), the additional model complexity of GRU (21× more parameters)\n    only increases overfitting. This finding is strengthened by being replicated across\n    architectures: it''s not that GRU fails on a specific model, but that the data\n    regime makes complex temporal models counterproductive. This directly preempts\n    reviewer concern #1 about method novelty — simplicity isn''t a limitation, it''s\n    the correct choice given the data-method trade-off.'\n","numLines":776,"startLine":1,"totalLines":776}}}
